-- 091: Liseberg, Hansa-Park and Michigan's Adventure from RCDB via Carter's
-- screenshots, 2026-10-31, plus the relocations those pages list (Carter: "make
-- sure relocations are working properly too as you see them").
-- Stats fill bare rows only (guarded on no length; Woodstock Express, which RCDB
-- gives no length, on no height). New rows: Cirkusexpressen (1977-2008),
-- Kanonen (2005-2016), HangOver (1997-2002) at Liseberg; Cornwall Coaster
-- (2026) and Seeschlange (1977-1992) at Hansa-Park; Big Dipper (1999-2019) at
-- Michigan's Adventure.
-- Model names: maker-first as elsewhere. New ones: "Preston & Barbieri Mini
-- Coaster" (Stampbanan, Kleiner Zar - same Mine Vagon layout), "Gerstlauer
-- Family Coaster" (Cornwall Coaster, Schlange von Midgard), "Arrow Corkscrew".
-- Relocations linked (same_ride, 023; home = where it stands now):
--   Kanonen (Liseberg) -> Matugani (Lost Island); Matugani gets Kanonen's track stats.
--   HangOver (Liseberg) -> Triops (Bagatelle); Allou Fun Park and Sommerland
--     Syd stops are not parks here.
--   Big Dipper -> Woodstock Express (same park, moved into Camp Snoopy 2020).
--   Thriller (Groena Lund 1996) -> Texas Tornado (AstroWorld 1998), as the
--     Thriller page said (089/090).
-- Not linked, partner not in the database: Cirkusexpressen (-> Achtbaan, Mondo
-- Verde), Seeschlange (-> Colorado Express, Varde Sommerland; Achterbahn, Magic
-- Park Verden), Thunderhawk (<- Geauga Lake).
-- Names kept as stored (Kleiner Zar, Die Schlange von Midgard). Safe to run twice.
